From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 06:33:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] census: held pages are read-only, so a CPU store reaches
 QEMU

A store to a uffd-wp page in a writable VMA, with guest interrupts on and an
in-kernel LAPIC, never left KVM: GUP failed, hva_to_pfn saw a valid VMA and
answered NEEDS_IO, KVM took the async page fault path, whose worker failed in
turn and was ignored, and the vCPU retried for ever with no exit to userspace.
Every user-mode store to a held page has hung since the first coherent build.
Only MercuryPosterExtension hit it because few CPU codes write GPU-made pixels.

Held and armed pages now live in a read-only VMA from the moment they are
tracked: vma_is_valid is false, and KVM gives -EFAULT at once. An armed page in
a read-only VMA also fails before its poison, so census_coh_probe arms held
pages and makes armed ones writable, and the rerun's SIGBUS gives the address.
Nothing can land between marks, so hold reports nothing and the pagemap goes.

The -EFAULT fuse no longer runs for a try that lost its page to a hold: 1290
such tries in 20 ms tripped it in the race test under load.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
